  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Match List I with List II :</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 600px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td><strong>List I</strong></td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td><strong>List II</strong></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>A</td>\t\t\t<td>Isothermal Process</td>\t\t\t<td>I</td>\t\t\t<td>Work done by the gas decreases internal energy</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>B</td>\t\t\t<td>Adiabatic Process</td>\t\t\t<td>II</td>\t\t\t<td>No change in internal energy</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>C</td>\t\t\t<td>Isochoric Process</td>\t\t\t<td>III</td>\t\t\t<td>The heat absorbed goes partly to increase internal energy and partly to do work</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>D</td>\t\t\t<td>Isobaric Process</td>\t\t\t<td>IV</td>\t\t\t<td>No work is done on or by the gas</td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below :</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "A-II, B-I, C-III, D-IV",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "A-II, B-I, C-IV, D-III",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "A-I, B-II, C-IV, D-III",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "A-I, B-II, C-III, D-IV",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>(A) Change in internal energy is expressed as<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>T</mi></math>, here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>T</mi></math>&nbsp;is change in temperature.</p><p>Since, in an isothermal process temperature remains&nbsp;constant, thus,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>I</mi><mi>I</mi></math></p><p>(B) In an adiabatic process, heat transfer,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p><p>So, from first law of thermodynamics,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>W</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>W</mi></math></p><p>Since, work done by gas is positive, thus,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>U</mi></math> is negative</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>I</mi></math></p><p>(C) In an isochoric process, volume remains constant, so work done by or on the gas&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>W</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>I</mi><mi>V</mi></math></p><p>(D) In an isobaric process, pressure remains constant, so work done<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;change in internal energy&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Thus, heat absorbed goes partly to increase internal energy and partly do work.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>I</mi><mi>I</mi><mi>I</mi></math></p>"
  }
